WEBVTT

00:01.406 --> 00:04.868
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.902 --> 00:08.171
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.172 --> 00:11.741
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.776 --> 00:14.778
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.812 --> 00:18.248
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.282 --> 00:21.418
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.452 --> 00:23.019
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.054 --> 00:24.658
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.660 --> 00:30.198
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:41.983 --> 00:44.351
Brian, why are you dressed like a douche

00:44.386 --> 00:46.454
who hangs out with multiracial friends

00:46.488 --> 00:48.556
in a McDonald's commercial?

00:48.590 --> 00:50.057
Okay.

00:50.092 --> 00:51.402
All right, that'll do.

00:51.436 --> 00:53.394
Well, I'm heading out. See y'all.

00:53.428 --> 00:55.206
Hey, Brian, that hat
makes you look like a wang.

00:55.208 --> 00:57.832
Squat and white
with a dark mushroom cap,

00:57.866 --> 01:00.267
- like Michael Jackson.
- Is that true?

01:01.703 --> 01:02.714
Yes.

01:02.716 --> 01:05.706
Let me guess, Bri.
You're off to try and get laid

01:05.741 --> 01:07.875
- at some sad nightclub.
- Shut up, Stewie.

01:07.909 --> 01:09.376
I'm not just out for sex.

01:09.411 --> 01:12.413
I want a woman who I can spend
the rest of my life with.

01:12.447 --> 01:13.812
I simply haven't found her yet.

01:13.814 --> 01:16.217
And you never will, because the truth is

01:16.251 --> 01:19.220
you're a selfish horndog who's
getting too old for the game.

01:19.254 --> 01:22.022
I beg to differ.
I think I've got the lingo

01:22.057 --> 01:24.225
of today's lady down pat.

01:24.259 --> 01:27.928
Hey. Might I Pinterest you
in a drink-point-oh?

01:35.003 --> 01:37.171
Ladies.

01:37.205 --> 01:39.840
How about the Verizon guy
moving over to Sprint? Huh?

01:39.875 --> 01:41.842
That seems kind of wack, right?

01:41.877 --> 01:44.912
- Like, zero chill.
- I can't understand you.

01:44.946 --> 01:47.197
Does anyone here speak Old Dude?

01:47.198 --> 01:49.950
Is Bernie Sanders here bothering you?

01:53.221 --> 01:54.855
Another bourbon, please.

01:54.890 --> 01:56.824
- Shut up, dick.
- Wha...?

01:56.858 --> 01:59.627
- Why do I come here?
- Tell me about it.

01:59.661 --> 02:02.429
<i>He called me a dick earlier.</i>

02:02.464 --> 02:04.532
- I'm Jess.
- Thanks. I'm Brian.

02:04.566 --> 02:06.267
Well, Jess, bottoms up.

02:06.301 --> 02:08.469
If you're lucky.

02:09.271 --> 02:11.438
So, this place, uh...

02:11.473 --> 02:13.674
it's worse than Syria, don't you think?

02:13.708 --> 02:16.018
Yes! Everything about it is awful.

02:16.020 --> 02:17.511
The people, the music...

02:17.546 --> 02:19.713
- If you can call it music.
- If you can call it music.

02:19.748 --> 02:22.616
Oh, my God, we were grumpy
and bitter at the same time.

02:22.651 --> 02:25.119
I like you, Brian.

02:25.153 --> 02:27.388
You actually say what's on your mind.

02:27.422 --> 02:28.956
Hey, life's too short, right?

02:28.990 --> 02:29.992
Tell me about it.

02:30.032 --> 02:32.834
I've been diagnosed
with non-Hodgkin's lymphoma.

02:32.869 --> 02:34.870
Oh, you know, cancer?

02:34.904 --> 02:36.972
<i>Oh, my God, I thought I smelled cancer.</i>

02:37.006 --> 02:38.974
Still want to go back to my place?

02:39.008 --> 02:41.410
Sounds great. Or, as young people say,

02:41.444 --> 02:43.445
"Hashtag yes!"

02:55.494 --> 02:57.628
- Whew!
- That was incredible.

02:57.663 --> 03:00.464
And hey, sorry I barked
when you took your pants off.

03:00.499 --> 03:02.066
I thought it was a squirrel.

03:02.100 --> 03:03.200
Ready to go again?

03:03.235 --> 03:04.535
Oh, I need time.

03:04.569 --> 03:06.804
I'm still recovering
from that one thing you did

03:06.838 --> 03:09.140
that was so obscene,
it couldn't even be described

03:09.174 --> 03:11.342
on lame, dying network TV.

03:11.376 --> 03:12.686
Have you always been so...

03:12.688 --> 03:15.479
Freaky? No. But when I got my diagnosis,

03:15.514 --> 03:19.350
I made a bucket list
of wild sex stuff I want to try.

03:19.909 --> 03:22.820
Jess, I would like
to help you cross offos

03:22.854 --> 03:24.922
every single item on this list.

03:24.956 --> 03:27.158
Aw. You would do that for me?

03:27.192 --> 03:28.793
All except for number 17.

03:28.827 --> 03:30.194
I'm allergic to chocolate.

03:30.228 --> 03:32.530
But isn't that only I?

03:32.564 --> 03:35.666
You know what? Let me make a phone call.

03:46.211 --> 03:47.845
<i>Oh...</i>

03:51.083 --> 03:53.084
<i>Yeah!</i>

04:13.772 --> 04:15.806
Brian, I'm glad
your girlfriend could join us

04:15.841 --> 04:17.875
- for dinner tonight.
- Thanks, Lois.

04:17.909 --> 04:19.877
And when she gets back
from the bathroom,

04:19.911 --> 04:21.879
<i>none of you say anything about cancer.</i>

04:21.913 --> 04:24.081
I'm serious. I really enjoy
spending time with this woman,

04:24.116 --> 04:26.217
and I don't want you ruining it for me.

04:26.251 --> 04:28.219
- Okay, okay, promise.
- Of course. We got it.

04:28.253 --> 04:29.920
Lois, you didn't have to go
through all this trouble.

04:29.955 --> 04:32.923
It's like a whole Thanksgiving dinner.

04:32.958 --> 04:34.525
Oh, it's no problem, Jess.

04:34.559 --> 04:36.127
We're happy to have you.

04:36.161 --> 04:38.429
Chris, pass me a turkey leg, would you?

04:38.463 --> 04:40.097
I prefer the limbs.

04:40.132 --> 04:42.666
I got a "limb fo' Ma."

04:42.701 --> 04:45.603
Uh, let's stop talking
about the food. All right?

04:45.637 --> 04:47.705
Anyone seen any good movies lately?

04:47.739 --> 04:49.373
I saw that new Tom Hanks movie.

04:49.407 --> 04:51.375
Oh, man, I love every Tom Hanks movie,

04:51.409 --> 04:53.043
<i>except The Terminal.</i>

04:53.078 --> 04:55.045
There's nothing worse than
when you're flipping channels,

04:55.080 --> 04:57.047
<i>and you're like,
"Oh, God, it's Terminal.</i>

04:57.082 --> 04:58.315
<i>"Don't say it's Terminal.</i>

04:58.350 --> 05:00.217
"God, what have I done to deserve this?

05:00.252 --> 05:02.219
<i>Why does it have to be Terminal?!"</i>

05:02.254 --> 05:05.189
Sir, I will tell you
a great Tom Hanks movie:

05:05.223 --> 05:07.491
<i>Catch Me If You Can, sir.</i>

05:07.526 --> 05:09.593
You have literally
never called Peter "sir."

05:09.628 --> 05:12.096
<i>Well, I've never told you
that I can't throw a boomerang,</i>

05:12.130 --> 05:13.464
but it's true.

05:19.311 --> 05:21.445
See? I told you. But at least
I don't have cancer,

05:21.479 --> 05:23.280
- like your girlfriend.
- That's it.

05:23.315 --> 05:25.015
I'm getting you out ofere.

05:30.088 --> 05:32.590
I like your family. They're scumbags.

05:32.624 --> 05:34.625
I like you.

05:35.660 --> 05:37.194
No, Jess...

05:37.228 --> 05:39.029
I really like you.

05:39.064 --> 05:42.066
I can't remember the last time
I felt this happy.

05:51.076 --> 05:52.710
I feel dizzy.

05:52.744 --> 05:54.044
Me, too.

05:54.079 --> 05:56.380
This all happened so fast, I...

05:56.414 --> 05:58.048
Jess? Are you okay?

06:00.018 --> 06:01.085
Jess?

06:01.119 --> 06:03.087
Are you guys still leaving?

06:03.121 --> 06:05.122
Oh. Yeah. Sorry.

06:18.603 --> 06:19.903
Wait, where's Dr. Hartman?

06:19.938 --> 06:21.905
I'm afraid Jess's condition
is too serious

06:21.940 --> 06:23.907
to be announced by Dr. Hartman.

06:23.942 --> 06:26.243
So they sent me, Dr. Gravitas.

06:26.277 --> 06:28.345
- Oh... boy.
- Uh-oh.

06:28.380 --> 06:30.247
Jess, I'll come right out and say it.

06:30.281 --> 06:32.116
The cancer did not respond to treatment

06:32.150 --> 06:34.251
and has spread throughout your body.

06:34.285 --> 06:36.787
You've got approximately
two weeks left to live.

06:36.821 --> 06:38.288
Oh, my God.

06:38.323 --> 06:39.657
Oh...

06:41.292 --> 06:43.360
I'm so sorry, Jess.

06:43.395 --> 06:45.229
If there's anything I can do...

06:45.263 --> 06:46.730
No, you've been great.

06:46.765 --> 06:49.533
I mean, you don't even
need to be here right now.

06:49.567 --> 06:50.934
I'm just some woman

06:50.969 --> 06:53.537
who never got to have
the career she wanted

06:53.571 --> 06:55.806
or get married or have kids.

06:58.510 --> 07:01.645
<i>One of those things... you can do.</i>

07:01.680 --> 07:03.280
It would be my honor

07:03.314 --> 07:05.282
if you spent the rest of your life

07:05.316 --> 07:06.684
as my bride.

07:06.718 --> 07:09.353
Oh, Brian. Yes!

07:14.659 --> 07:16.293
Oh, this is my vet.

07:16.327 --> 07:17.695
Hello?

07:17.729 --> 07:18.996
Oh, great.

07:19.030 --> 07:20.364
Well, some good news.

07:20.398 --> 07:22.733
That chocolate thing
from the bucket list?

07:22.767 --> 07:24.768
We're all good. Let's do it.

07:24.803 --> 07:28.038
Toblerone probably isn't
the best thing for this.

07:36.130 --> 07:38.298
Brian? It would mean the world to me

07:38.332 --> 07:40.934
if you wore my tux
from when I got married.

07:40.968 --> 07:42.269
I love you, buddy.

07:42.303 --> 07:44.638
Yeah, I'm not wearing
a fat guy's old clothes.

07:44.672 --> 07:47.908
And... Wha... Is this a flap
on the butt of these pants?

07:47.942 --> 07:49.743
Yup. In case of emergencies.

07:49.777 --> 07:51.778
My invention. Called it the Suit-Chute.

07:51.812 --> 07:54.281
Got it patented in '97
and went into business.

07:54.315 --> 07:56.416
Shot a local commercial and everything.

07:56.450 --> 07:58.518
I'm Peter Griffin,
inventor of the Suit-Chute.

07:58.552 --> 08:00.253
Are you about to walk down the aisle

08:00.288 --> 08:01.454
and afraid you'll leave it brown?

08:01.489 --> 08:03.623
Did you eat creamy soup
just before the opera?

08:03.658 --> 08:05.792
Are you George Brett
at an awards ceremony?

08:05.826 --> 08:07.928
Then you need a tux with the Suit-Chute.

08:07.962 --> 08:09.629
<i>Don't take my word for it.</i>

08:09.664 --> 08:13.466
Ask famous Hollywood actor-
slash-pants filler Dennis Franz.

08:13.501 --> 08:15.802
<i>On NYPD Blue,
I'm known for packin' heat.</i>

08:15.836 --> 08:18.271
But every year when I go to the Emmys,

08:18.306 --> 08:21.474
the heat I'm packin'
is clumpy and smells terrible.

08:21.509 --> 08:24.044
Not anymore, thanks to the Suit-Chute.

08:24.078 --> 08:25.812
And the winner is...

08:25.846 --> 08:28.148
your socks and shoes.

08:31.786 --> 08:34.354
The business died,
and I lost $200,000, Brian.

08:34.388 --> 08:35.622
Want to know why?

08:35.656 --> 08:38.525
"555" means it is not
an actual phone number.

08:38.559 --> 08:40.827
I truly wish I had known that.

08:42.964 --> 08:45.198
Brian, I want nothing to do
with this sham wedding.

08:45.481 --> 08:48.217
So if you're going to ask me
to be your best man, don't.

08:48.251 --> 08:50.285
I'm not. I want you to be
the ring bearer,

08:50.320 --> 08:51.954
and wear a vest and a boutonniere

08:51.988 --> 08:54.356
- and carry a satin pillow...
- Sold, sold. Yes, I'm in.

08:54.390 --> 08:55.891
But it's still wrong. There's no way

08:55.925 --> 08:58.126
you'd be marrying this woman
if she wasn't going to die

08:58.161 --> 08:59.535
- in two weeks.
- Oh, come on!

08:59.614 --> 09:01.281
Did you know that Lois was so moved

09:01.315 --> 09:04.317
she called Channel Five
to do a profile of me and Jess?

09:04.352 --> 09:07.721
And now get out your tissues,
it's a real-life Quahog version

09:07.755 --> 09:09.556
<i>of The Fault in Our Stars,</i>

09:09.590 --> 09:13.093
the novel and hit movie your
gay nephew quotes on Facebook.

09:15.129 --> 09:16.930
<i>My name is Jess.</i>

09:16.964 --> 09:18.465
<i>I have cancer.</i>

09:18.499 --> 09:21.268
<i>But cancer doesn't have me.</i>

09:21.302 --> 09:22.802
<i>My name is Brian.</i>

09:22.837 --> 09:24.271
<i>I have a disease...</i>

09:24.305 --> 09:25.939
<i>called love.</i>

09:25.973 --> 09:27.941
<i>It may have started in my penis,</i>

09:27.975 --> 09:30.243
<i>but it spread to my heart.</i>

09:35.549 --> 09:38.785
And, Brian, when you learned
Jess had only weeks to live,

09:38.819 --> 09:40.287
you proposed.

09:40.321 --> 09:42.122
Yep. Got in right under the wire.

09:42.156 --> 09:45.158
No one's ever loved me like Brian does.

09:45.192 --> 09:48.695
You know, sometimes at night I
just watch Jess sleep for hours.

09:48.729 --> 09:51.097
And I go, "Hey. Hey, you alive?"

09:51.132 --> 09:53.800
And she says, "Yeah," and
then I go, "All right, good."

09:53.834 --> 09:55.802
I'm, uh... I'm sorry.

09:55.836 --> 09:59.306
I'm sorry to be a puss.

10:00.908 --> 10:02.309
Hey, pal.

10:02.343 --> 10:04.577
Listen, I kn-I know
we've had our differences,

10:04.612 --> 10:07.580
- but you're a good guy.
- Thank you, Quagmire.

10:07.615 --> 10:10.183
Listen, I want to throw you
the wildest bachelor party

10:10.217 --> 10:12.218
of all time. It's gonna be crazier

10:12.253 --> 10:15.355
than whatever Kanye West is
doing at this particular moment.

10:15.389 --> 10:17.657
I'm giving this lasagna a massage

10:17.692 --> 10:20.126
while preparing to announce
I'm joining ISIS.

10:20.161 --> 10:22.195
Thank you for your interest.

10:26.701 --> 10:28.501
This is delicious.

10:28.536 --> 10:30.503
Hmm. I still think the butter cream

10:30.538 --> 10:32.539
was the best cake I've thrown up so far.

10:32.573 --> 10:34.874
Oh, speaking of which. Mwah!

10:36.177 --> 10:38.211
Excuse me, I don't mean to bother you.

10:38.245 --> 10:41.014
A-Are you the dog
who's marrying the cancer girl?

10:41.048 --> 10:42.916
Oh, uh, yeah, I am.

10:42.950 --> 10:45.352
Oh, my God, we saw you
on the news last night!

10:45.386 --> 10:47.721
You are just the best person.
I can't even.

10:47.755 --> 10:49.189
How's she doing?

10:49.223 --> 10:50.457
Honestly, not well.

10:50.491 --> 10:52.425
She's only got ten days.

10:52.460 --> 10:55.028
So in ten days you'll be alone?

10:55.062 --> 10:56.396
I guess.

10:56.430 --> 10:58.031
Well, maybe not.

10:58.065 --> 10:59.532
I'll give you my number.

10:59.567 --> 11:02.235
Here, I'll put my number in
with my tongue.

11:02.269 --> 11:05.372
Eh, eh, eh, eh, eh.

11:05.406 --> 11:07.240
I'm not sure that's a complete number,

11:07.274 --> 11:10.410
but I'm gonna call you first.

11:10.444 --> 11:11.945
Wow. I haven't gotten
this kind of attention

11:11.979 --> 11:14.214
<i>since I went to see The Peanuts Movie.</i>

11:15.516 --> 11:16.783
- Look.
- There he is.

11:16.817 --> 11:18.084
That's him.

11:18.119 --> 11:21.321
That's the guy who peed
in his empty soda cup.

11:29.930 --> 11:32.565
Hello, Brian, I'm Jess's mother, Helen.

11:32.600 --> 11:34.000
Oh, hey.

11:34.035 --> 11:35.769
L-Listen, I've been
wanting to talk to you.

11:35.803 --> 11:38.571
I-I was thinking maybe you could
move in with me and Jess,

11:38.606 --> 11:41.641
because I-I know you'd want to
be with her for her final days.

11:41.675 --> 11:43.243
Well, now, thank you, Brian.

11:43.277 --> 11:46.212
That is such a sweet offer.
I would love to be there.

11:46.247 --> 11:47.914
Now, you have a blessed day.

11:47.948 --> 11:50.817
Oh... Oh, no.

11:55.489 --> 11:57.090
We's all gathered here

11:57.124 --> 12:00.460
to join this couple in holy matrimony.

12:00.494 --> 12:02.128
Yet another wedding

12:02.163 --> 12:04.798
I'm on this side of, Jeffrey.

12:06.467 --> 12:08.835
We's just waiting for his mama to die.

12:08.869 --> 12:10.970
We've written our own vows.

12:11.005 --> 12:12.639
Oh, no.

12:12.673 --> 12:15.275
Brian, I...
I haven't known you that long.

12:15.309 --> 12:16.676
But these past weeks

12:16.710 --> 12:19.946
I feel like you've given me
a lifetime of love.

12:19.980 --> 12:22.282
I vow to honor you and cherish you

12:22.316 --> 12:24.284
until the day I die,

12:24.318 --> 12:26.052
a week from Wednesday.

12:26.087 --> 12:28.822
I'm so happy to place this ring

12:28.856 --> 12:32.459
on the weird dog thumb you have
halfway up your arm.

12:36.831 --> 12:40.266
Jess, I wish we had
a million years together.

12:40.301 --> 12:42.268
But what we have is this moment,

12:42.303 --> 12:44.871
and I wouldn't trade it for anything.

12:44.905 --> 12:48.808
With this ring, I vow to honor
you and cherish you...

12:48.843 --> 12:50.810
for the rest of the month.

12:50.845 --> 12:54.814
Ma'am, do you take this doggie
to be your husband?

12:54.849 --> 12:56.149
I do.

12:56.183 --> 12:57.317
Yay!

12:57.351 --> 12:58.485
How about you, doggie?

12:58.519 --> 12:59.652
Samesies?

12:59.687 --> 13:02.322
- I do.
- Yay, again!

13:02.356 --> 13:04.524
By the power bottom vested in me,

13:04.558 --> 13:07.660
I now pronounce y'all husband and wife.

13:07.695 --> 13:09.195
Kiss!

13:10.531 --> 13:13.299
Aw.

13:17.371 --> 13:19.906
Everyone! Your attention, please!

13:19.940 --> 13:21.407
Dr. Gravitas?

13:21.442 --> 13:22.509
That's right.

13:22.543 --> 13:24.811
I want to give you two your first gift.

13:24.845 --> 13:26.679
These are your latest
test results, Jess.

13:26.714 --> 13:27.881
And they're remarkable.

13:27.915 --> 13:29.048
Meaning what?

13:29.083 --> 13:32.452
Meaning Jess... is going to live.

13:37.224 --> 13:40.527
<i>Brian, we really
will be together forever.</i>

13:40.561 --> 13:43.696
Forever and ever and ever!

13:45.566 --> 13:47.534
Can you believe this?

13:47.568 --> 13:49.002
What?

13:49.036 --> 13:50.837
Jess is gonna live.

13:50.871 --> 13:53.206
I-I'm sorry, I took a-a muscle
relaxer this morning.

13:53.240 --> 13:54.507
Tinazidine.

13:54.542 --> 13:56.342
Before you drove here?!

13:56.377 --> 13:58.378
Yeah, I took half of one
before I got in the car.

13:58.412 --> 14:00.046
And then another half at a red light.

14:00.080 --> 14:01.381
It's fine, it's Tinazidine.

14:01.415 --> 14:02.715
I-I might take another half.

14:02.750 --> 14:03.783
You want a half?

14:03.817 --> 14:06.085
Oh, no.

14:06.120 --> 14:08.421
Come on. It was prescribed by a doctor

14:08.455 --> 14:10.557
to a guy named John Selvaggio

14:10.591 --> 14:13.026
who has a mailbox that he can't
see from his front yard.

14:13.060 --> 14:14.227
It's Tinazidine.

14:14.261 --> 14:15.662
Stop saying what it is.

14:15.696 --> 14:17.197
<i>Tinazidine:</i>

14:17.231 --> 14:19.165
<i>the white, plastic pouch
in your neighbor's mailbox</i>

14:19.200 --> 14:21.634
<i>that might be three months of drugs.</i>

14:30.451 --> 14:33.419
Oh, my God. It is so incredible

14:33.454 --> 14:35.455
having my appetite back.

14:35.489 --> 14:37.023
Mm.

14:37.057 --> 14:39.092
I love you.

14:39.126 --> 14:40.493
Ah, shrimp.

14:40.527 --> 14:41.928
It's like I'm a baby bird.

14:45.165 --> 14:48.268
This turn me on, too.

14:54.975 --> 14:56.342
Brian, did you hear that?

14:56.377 --> 14:57.477
Mm-hmm.

14:57.511 --> 14:58.945
Remember what the doctor said?

14:58.979 --> 15:02.949
Flatulence means my digestive
system is working again.

15:02.983 --> 15:05.718
Oh, my God, I must have, like,

15:05.753 --> 15:08.655
six months worth
of cancer-farts built up.

15:19.833 --> 15:21.467
Would you stop farting, please?

15:21.502 --> 15:23.836
This is a nice hotel.

15:27.174 --> 15:29.842
Okay, that's the last box.

15:29.877 --> 15:32.745
Aw, you're so glad to be back
with me, aren't you?

15:32.780 --> 15:34.347
Mommy was so sad

15:34.381 --> 15:36.949
when she had to put you all
up for adoption.

15:36.984 --> 15:38.618
Yes, she was.

15:38.652 --> 15:40.987
Ooh, I'm going straight to the kitchen

15:41.021 --> 15:43.456
to make my favorite meal
in a tiny apartment:

15:43.490 --> 15:45.591
microwaved salmon.

15:50.864 --> 15:52.665
Welcome back, Brian.

15:52.700 --> 15:54.801
That's Lou,

15:54.835 --> 15:57.537
the apartment manager
from when Brian moved out.

15:57.571 --> 16:00.206
Ain't that somethin'
to flip your biscuit.

16:02.242 --> 16:03.609
What?

16:03.644 --> 16:05.244
That's my thing I say, remember?

16:05.279 --> 16:06.512
Oh. Uh, no.

16:06.547 --> 16:08.681
I-I can't imagine anyone does.

16:08.716 --> 16:10.183
Hey, listen, thanks for renting to us

16:10.217 --> 16:12.685
even though we have ten cats and
couldn't make the deposit.

16:12.720 --> 16:15.488
Spent, uh, pretty much
every last penny on our wedding.

16:15.522 --> 16:17.023
Dead broke.

16:17.057 --> 16:19.525
Ain't that somethin'
to flip your biscuit.

16:24.932 --> 16:27.967
So, Bri, this...

16:28.001 --> 16:30.536
So, Bri, this is once again
your hellhole.

16:30.571 --> 16:32.338
I was going to help you move in

16:32.373 --> 16:35.007
but you don't really
own anything, do you?

16:35.042 --> 16:36.809
Yeah, we didn't bother
to register for giftsis

16:36.844 --> 16:39.212
because she was supposed to die!

16:39.246 --> 16:41.748
I must say, she's looking... healthy.

16:41.782 --> 16:44.217
Putting those Juicy pants to the test.

16:44.251 --> 16:46.119
Stewie, I've got to get out of this.

16:46.153 --> 16:47.387
You were right all along, okay?

16:47.421 --> 16:48.721
I'm not ready to be married.

16:48.756 --> 16:50.490
I-I gotta... I gotta get a divorce.

16:50.524 --> 16:52.392
Oh, that'll go over well
after you paraded

16:52.426 --> 16:54.727
your "great love" around town.

16:54.762 --> 16:57.096
Which reminds me, your
follow-up Tom Tucker profile

16:57.131 --> 16:58.731
is coming on now.

16:58.766 --> 17:00.099
We got countless letters

17:00.134 --> 17:02.034
after our profile of the Cancer Girl

17:02.069 --> 17:04.570
who won her sweetheart's paw
in marriage.

17:04.605 --> 17:07.407
Turns out their story
has a very happy ending.

17:07.441 --> 17:10.743
Due to audio issues, the
following footage is subtitled.

17:44.378 --> 17:45.645
Brian, look.

17:47.714 --> 17:49.282
- Holy...
- I know.

17:49.316 --> 17:50.983
My hair's growing back.

17:51.018 --> 17:52.852
What do you think?

17:52.886 --> 17:55.922
You look like a baby doll
found in hurricane rubble.

17:55.956 --> 17:58.391
Aw, I'm your baby doll.

17:58.425 --> 18:00.460
I'll get it.

18:00.494 --> 18:03.963
Ain't that somethin'
to flip your biscuit?

18:03.997 --> 18:05.798
Nothing?

18:07.835 --> 18:10.303
Oh, hey, Helen. What are you doing here?

18:10.337 --> 18:12.972
Coming to live with you, like
you asked me to at the wedding.

18:13.006 --> 18:15.107
Are-are you watching HBO?

18:15.142 --> 18:16.943
I'm a Christian woman, Brian.

18:16.977 --> 18:18.744
Cancel HBO now.

18:18.779 --> 18:20.146
We can spend the extra money

18:20.180 --> 18:21.981
on the big photos of fetuses I hold

18:22.015 --> 18:24.851
while I yell at people outside Panera.

18:24.885 --> 18:26.185
Mom, guess what?

18:26.220 --> 18:28.354
My farts are back.

18:28.388 --> 18:31.023
Mine never went away.

18:31.058 --> 18:33.392
Oh, man.

18:36.797 --> 18:39.832
- Uh-huh.
- So the crazy ex-girlfriend

18:39.867 --> 18:42.535
- sings this hilarious song.
- Uh-huh.

18:42.569 --> 18:44.270
It's all about how
she's having her period,

18:44.304 --> 18:46.005
but the other guy
she wanted to impress...

18:46.039 --> 18:47.874
The one who created
the social media app...

18:47.908 --> 18:49.442
He walks in while she's singing,

18:49.476 --> 18:51.844
<i>so now he's not into her, either.</i>

18:51.879 --> 18:53.179
Uh-huh.

18:55.349 --> 18:58.584
- Will you get me more salsa?
- Uh-huh.

18:58.619 --> 19:00.186
Brian.

19:00.220 --> 19:02.188
Will you get me more salsa?

19:02.224 --> 19:04.750
Huh? Sorry. Got it.

19:11.265 --> 19:12.899
They only had mild.

19:16.937 --> 19:19.005
<i>Well, I'm sorry it's so disgusting,</i>

19:19.039 --> 19:21.040
but that's all they have.

19:21.074 --> 19:23.709
Oh, you're gonna die if you
have to eat mild salsa?

19:23.744 --> 19:25.311
Come on.

19:27.314 --> 19:29.348
Wait, are you... Oh, my G...

19:29.383 --> 19:31.250
Oh, my God, are you choking?

19:31.285 --> 19:33.486
She's... Someone... I don't...

19:33.520 --> 19:34.987
Heimlich maneuver.

19:35.022 --> 19:36.522
How do you do the Heimlich maneuver?

19:36.524 --> 19:37.924
Come on, come on.

19:37.958 --> 19:40.693
Damn it. I've got one song
by Haim on my phone?

19:40.727 --> 19:42.595
And every time I try to type
"Heimlich", it...

19:50.070 --> 19:52.538
Oh, my God. Somebody call 911!

19:52.573 --> 19:53.973
Damn it, Fox.

19:54.007 --> 19:56.008
That's not an invitation
to ruin our moment

19:56.043 --> 19:58.477
to expand your media empire.

20:00.380 --> 20:02.915
<i>Son of Zorn.</i>

20:02.950 --> 20:04.750
Ha.

20:23.555 --> 20:25.322
I'd like to thank you all for coming

20:25.356 --> 20:29.126
to honor the memory
of my beloved wife Jess...

20:29.160 --> 20:30.694
Uh...

20:30.728 --> 20:33.897
I'm sorry, I'm just realizing
I never caught her last name.

20:33.932 --> 20:35.532
- Schlotz.
- Yikes.

20:35.567 --> 20:37.034
It was my husband's name.

20:37.068 --> 20:38.202
What's your maiden name?

20:38.236 --> 20:39.369
Borgwort.

20:39.404 --> 20:41.038
That's also bad.

20:41.072 --> 20:43.373
Look, all I want to say is...

20:43.408 --> 20:45.876
I always knew this day was coming.

20:45.910 --> 20:47.845
But what I didn't know was...

20:47.879 --> 20:50.314
just how much I was gonna miss Jess.

20:50.348 --> 20:52.516
I would give anything

20:52.550 --> 20:54.718
if she were still here with me.

20:56.588 --> 20:57.888
I'm okay.

20:57.922 --> 20:59.756
It's a miracle!

21:02.912 --> 21:06.418
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv